    style(scan-scope): wrap the audit-scope FAIL print for ruff format (CF-163)
    
    The tree's only ruff-unformatted file was introduced by 5794a49 (CF-163 AC3):
    one `print(f"  FAIL  audit-scope: ...")` line does not fit the default 88-column
    budget, so `ruff format --check .` answered "1 file would be reformatted"
    on every releng pass since. Whitespace only — the same f-string, the same
    exit codes, no behaviour change.
    
    Re-run:
      ruff format --check .                      -> 15 files already formatted
      ruff check .                               -> All checks passed!
      python3 scripts/check_scan_scope.py        -> OK  audit-scope: 7 claims,
                                                    RESULT: OK, rc 0
      bash tests/selftest.sh                     -> SELFTEST: PASS, rc 0 (106 rows)
    
    Note: ruff is not a declared gate in this repo (no pyproject/ruff.toml, no
    selftest arm, no AGENTS.md line). This is lane-checklist conformance from the
    releng gate battery, not a repo gate failure; disclosed so nobody reads a
    green format leg as evidence the repo ships a formatter check.
    
    Suite flake observed while gating this commit: one run at this exact tree
    graded section 7b's `number` arm FAIL ("number fixture escaped the board gate
    (exit 1)") while printing an output that satisfies every condition the arm
    tests; two further runs at the same tree answered SELFTEST: PASS / 106 rows.
    The arm did not reproduce in 20 isolated iterations. Assertion sites are
    tests/selftest.sh:242-244, which run `printf | grep -q` under `set -uo
    pipefail` — a construct that can return 141 when grep exits before printf
    finishes writing. Filed as a board row rather than fixed here (this commit is
    the format leg only).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
